+# CEO G2-A Implementation Plan
+
+Goal: M03–M06 synthetic-only cognition, analysis, task reads, workflow state and append-only trace.
+Spec: approved CEO_Agent_V1.0_Minimal_Change_Scope_20261105.md plus current G2-A authorization.
+Architecture: additive deterministic modules, existing G1 governance, host-supplied snapshots. No production adapters, executors, credentials or framework.
+Constraints: store 400370; preserve all G1 files and other worktrees; exact dictionaries 1.0.0/1.1.0 as fixtures; no formal DB/log writes; no merge/deploy; stop after report.
+Review focus: forged VERIFIED facts; mixed periods and changed evidence; missing/WAL task DB; concurrent duplicate log writes; forged Human corrections and stale task refs.
+
+- [ ] Setup: new worktree + exact G1 snapshot, baseline hash protection and safe runner.
+- [ ] M03: ceo-vnext-context.js, ceo-vnext-analysis.js, cognition/source policy and JSON schemas. RED/GREEN for quality, evidence, period/store, 0/null, core version and three priorities.
+- [ ] M04: ceo-task-read-model.js reads existing synthetic SQLite with readOnly transaction and explicit failure; RED/GREEN no creation/initialization/WAL writes/cross-store/version mismatch.
+- [ ] M05: ceo-workflow-catalog.js and capabilities config; RED/GREEN unknown/stale/conflict/version and UNEXECUTED invocation analysis; executor calls zero.
+- [ ] M06: ceo-shadow-trace.js; synthetic append-only file, authorization before write, atomic concurrent dedup/restart, Human correction/pause, fail closed on corruption/write failures.
+- [ ] G2-A service composition: host-owned context/task/workflow injection, G1 authorize for read/analyze/feedback; report proposals never imported as tasks; link trace only after successful append.
+- [ ] Targeted independent review; address findings with tests; run G1/related regression and one isolated full suite comparison to 26 known failures.
+- [ ] Deliver report, all diffs/results/failures, protection hashes, G2-B minimum gates; stop.
+
+No design reconfirmation: user explicitly authorized autonomous planning, implementation, repair and retest within this scope. Independent M04/M06 edits are delegated to disjoint files using dispatching-parallel-agents; no shared-file edits or nested agents. No production startup changes.
